> > I can't get it to compile.  This [zipped] patch:
> >
> >   http://www.geocities.com/zindorsky/patches/photo.zip
> >
> > doesn't contain definitions for SCR_PHOTOGRAPH or SPE_PHOTO_ALBUM
> > anywhere.  Presumably they should be in "include/onames.h", but
> > surely someone should have noticed this before me?
>
> For your answer, look at the comment at the top of onames.h:
> /* This source file is generated by 'makedefs'.  Do not edit. */
>
> I'm don't know how 'makedefs' works, but I'd guess that it generates
> onames.h by processing files like objects.c which, you will note, _is_
> modified by the photo patch (and any patch that modifies objects).
>
> So your onames.h is not being updated by makedefs for some reason. Did
> you take it out of your makefile?

  No; in fact, I see that onames.h *is* being updated by the make
process.  I can tell because it gets generated with Unix linefeeds,
and if I convert the Unix linefeeds to MS-DOS linefeeds and 'make clean',
the Unix linefeeds come back.

> >   Also, the patch to "win/share/tilemap.c" is suspicious.  It
> > refers to SCR_PHOTOGRAPH and SPE_PHOTO_ALBUM even though they
> > haven't been defined at that point; I think it should be referring
> > to the tiles for some *other* object, to use as a default
> > representation in case that patch has *not* been compiled in.
> > Source divers' comments welcome.

  Changing 'SCR_PHOTOGRAPH' and 'SPE_PHOTO_ALBUM' both to
'SCR_STINKING_CLOUD+4' handles this problem.  Remember, this is
a problem when PHOTOGRAPHY is *not* #defined!  And it is an obvious
bug.
  Another bug in the photo patch is that there should be an
#ifdef PHOTOGRAPHY / #endif around the entire contents of 'photo.c',
after the line #include "hack.h".  This way, the Makefile doesn't
have to change if the user decides to remove PHOTOGRAPHY from
"config.h".

  I haven't tried yet to compile the whole thing with PHOTOGRAPHY
#defined; I want to make sure it integrates properly first.
